From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:13:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 082/105] C1 step 1: make the draft's real top-1 probability
 available

For topk=1 drafting neither producer of a draft token computed its
probability: draft_topk1_postprocess stored a constant 1.0 into topk_p
("chain probabilities are unused downstream") and _draft_extend_for_decode
used torch.argmax + ones_like.  The adaptive controller therefore had only
the historical acceptance EMA to decide chain length with.

- topk1.py: the split argmax already reads every logit, so each split now
  optionally also stores sum(exp(v - m_split)); the finalize kernel combines
  those into p_top1 = 1/sum_j s_j*exp(m_j - M) and writes it to a caller-owned
  (bs, steps) buffer column.  Gated by a tl.constexpr, so with chain_probs=None
  the kernels specialise back to the original code.  topk_p is deliberately
  left at 1.0 so every existing consumer is bit-identical.
- _draft_extend_for_decode computes the position-0 probability eagerly
  (logsumexp + amax over the hot vocab).  This is the only chain position
  whose confidence exists *before* the next step's state swap, because the
  draft loop itself is one captured CUDA graph.
- ConfidenceChannel stages both to pinned host memory on the current stream
  with per-slot events; nothing synchronises the producing stream.
- ConfidenceStepSlot decides by throughput, not by threshold: it inverts the
  observed mean accepted count into a per-position acceptance rate r (which,
  unlike the mean, is comparable across step counts), tracks r per position-0
  confidence bucket, and picks argmax_S (1 + E[accept|r,S]) / step_time(S).
- SGLANG_ADAPTIVE_POLICY=confidence selects it; default "ema" is unchanged.
  SGLANG_ADAPTIVE_TRACE=<path> dumps (steps, bs, chain probs, accepted) per
  step for offline simulation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
